# `Causal.Flat.AffACDTriang` — a nilpotent linear group generated by elements with spectrum near `1` is triangularizable, of class `≤ dim`

T. Barbot, *Globally hyperbolic flat space-times* (`papers/barbot`, arXiv math/0402257), §5,
Theorem 5.1 (`bthm:ausl`, `GHFspace.tex:1696`), in the printed generality (DEC-123). **No ledger
label is certified here**: this module is the UNIFORM CLASS BOUND of the affine route
(`Flat/AffACDLocal`), the step the survey (`docs/CARRIERE-DALBO-SURVEY.md` §2.2 T2) prices at
"a log chart, BCH and connected-subgroup theory, 3–6k lines". It is replaced here by elementary
linear algebra over `ℂ`; no Lie theory, no Zariski closure, no discreteness.

> Let $\Gamma$ be a discrete subgroup of $\mbox{Aff}(n, {\mathbb R})$.
> Then, the identity component $G_{0}$ of
> the closure of $L(\Gamma)$ in $GL(n, {\mathbb R})$ is nilpotent. (l.1699–1701)

## The mathematics (planner, 2026-11-08)

`G` a nilpotent group, `ρ : G → GL(W)`, `W` finite-dimensional over `ℂ`, `G = ⟨X⟩`, and every
eigenvalue `μ` of every `ρ(x)`, `x ∈ X`, has `|μ − 1| < 1` (`AffSpecNearOne`).

1. **Irreducible ⇒ `dim W = 1`** (`affacd_finrank_eq_one_of_irreducible`). Schur: a central
   element acts by a scalar. If every term `Z_i` of the upper central series acts by scalars,
   `ρ(G)` is scalar (`Z_c = G`) and `dim W = 1`. Otherwise take `i ≥ 2` minimal and `y ∈ Z_i`
   with `ρ(y)` not scalar. For `x ∈ G`, `[x, y] ∈ Z_{i−1}` acts by a scalar `c(x)`:
   `ρ(x) ρ(y) ρ(x)⁻¹ = c(x) ρ(y)`, and `det` gives `c(x)^m = 1`, `m = dim W`. If `c(x) = 1` for
   all `x ∈ X`, `ρ(y)` commutes with `ρ(⟨X⟩) = ρ(G)` and is scalar (Schur): so `c := c(x) ≠ 1`
   for some `x ∈ X`. For an eigenvalue `λ` of `ρ(x)` (eigenvector `v`), `ρ(y)ᵏ v` is an
   eigenvector for `cᵏ λ`, so every `cᵏ λ` is an eigenvalue and has `Re > 0` (`|cᵏλ − 1| < 1`).
   But `∑_{k<m} cᵏ λ = λ (cᵐ − 1)/(c − 1) = 0`, whose real part is `> 0`. Contradiction.
2. **A common eigenvector, then a complete invariant flag** (`affacd_exists_common_eigenvector`,
   `affacd_exists_flag`): a nonzero invariant subspace of least dimension is irreducible, so
   1-dimensional by (1) (its eigenvalues are eigenvalues of `ρ(x)`); then induct on `W ⧸ ℂv`
   (eigenvalues of the induced maps are eigenvalues of `ρ(x)`, `affacd_hasEigenvalue_of_mapQ`).
3. **Class bound** (`affacd_lowerCentralSeries_le_ker_of_flag`; nilpotency of `G` is used, the
   generators are not): for a complete invariant flag `F₀ = 0 < … < F_m = W` put
   `U_j = {g | (ρ g − 1) F_i ⊆ F_{i−j} ∀ i}`. `G ⧸ U₁` embeds in the diagonal `(ℂˣ)^m`, so
   `[G, G] ≤ U₁`. For `j ≥ 1`, `u ↦ (ρ u − 1) mod F_{i−j−1}` is additive on `U_j`, and conjugation
   by `x` multiplies its `(i, i−j)` entry by `χ_{i−j}(x) / χ_i(x)`; so the `k`-fold commutator
   `[x, [x, … u]]` has entry `(χ_{i−j}(x)/χ_i(x) − 1)ᵏ · (entry of u)`, which vanishes for `k` past
   the class of `G`; hence the ratio is `1` wherever the entry is nonzero, and `[x, u] ∈ U_{j+1}`.
   So `γ_{j+1}(G) ≤ U_j` and `γ_{m+1}(G) ≤ U_m = ker ρ`.
4. **Real form** (`affacd_lowerCentralSeries_eq_bot_of_near_one`): for `W` a finite-dimensional
   real normed space and `x ∈ GL(W)` with `‖x − 1‖ < 1/3`, every eigenvalue `μ` of the
   complexification `ℂ ⊗ x` has `|μ − 1| ≤ 3 ‖x − 1‖ < 1` (`affacd_norm_eigenvalue_baseChange_le`:
   for `B` real and `ν = a + ib` an eigenvalue of `ℂ ⊗ B`, `B² − 2aB + |ν|²` is not injective,
   while `‖B² − 2aB‖ ≤ ‖B‖² + 2|ν|‖B‖ < |ν|²` once `|ν| > 3‖B‖`, Neumann). The complexification
   is faithful, so a nilpotent `⟨X⟩ ≤ GL(W)` with `‖x − 1‖ < 1/3` on `X` has
   `γ_{dim W + 1} = 1`.

**Sanity checks.** `Q₈`, `D₈` and the generalized quaternion `Q_{2^k}` (whose class is
unbounded) are excluded exactly: each needs a generator with an eigenvalue `±i` or `−1`. The
unipotent triangular group of `GL_m` has class `m − 1 ≤ m`.

